-- id: exp6984-exact-contrast-fixture
-  title: Source-grouped exact mapping contrast fixture
-  track: verification
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: codex
-  model: gpt-5.6-sol
-  requires_gpu: false
-  max_turns: 50
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 90
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  milestone: 2026.09.612
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6984_exact_contrast_fixture.json
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    V611 froze 108 three-family mapping candidates and exactly certified every
-    row. Its calibration split had zero exact successes. Exp6977 could not fit
-    or certify a PWA-KAN from one-class labels. V612 first needs balanced,
-    source-grouped semantic contrasts. This fixture is controlled evidence. It
-    is not a live extraction-quality claim.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
-    - {project_root}/research-program.md
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6967_certified_error_headroom_fixture.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6975_delayed_constraint_candidate_bank.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6976_exact_candidate_certification.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6955_reformulation_fixture.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6957_smt_mapping_certification.json
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/experiment_6957_smt_mapping_certification.py
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/constraint-verification/spec.md
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/research-reporting/spec.md
-    - {project_root}/research-references.md V612 Planner Refresh
-
-    TASK:
-    Build a prospectively frozen exact mapping contrast fixture with one valid
-    candidate and one single-fault invalid candidate per source group. Blind
-    surface provenance, certify both members through independent authorities,
-    and freeze source-disjoint train, calibration, and held-out splits.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require the frozen V609 and V611 mapping schemas, Z3,
-       bounded enumeration, three supported formulation families, and writable
-       immutable row paths. On failure, write blocked_exact_contrast_fixture
-       with gate_check_summary.
-    1. Add REQ-VERIFY-6984 and RED tests before implementation. Cover label
-       balance, one-fault isolation, solver disagreement, source-group leakage,
-       alpha renaming, serialization blinding, and bare readiness fields.
-    2. Freeze 36 source groups before constructing candidates. Use 18 train,
-       six calibration, and 12 held-out groups. No source group may cross a
-       split. Record the manifest and hash before opening candidate labels.
-    3. Construct one exact positive mapping per group from the executable
-       specification. Construct one negative by applying exactly one frozen
-       fault: bound change, coefficient swap, objective-direction reversal, or
-       constraint omission. Preserve all attempted mutations.
-    4. Run Z3 and bounded enumeration on both candidates. Require agreement on
-       domain, satisfiability, optimum, objective order, and solution-space
-       relation. Unknown, timeout, disagreement, or multiple faults rejects the
-       pair without replacement from the held-out split.
-    5. Alpha-rename identifiers and canonicalize harmless formatting through a
-       label-blind function. Randomize pair order from the frozen seed. Keep the
-       unblinded source and mutation fields outside the future feature table.
-    6. Write raw candidate rows and exact authority rows before aggregate
-       metrics. Each split must contain both labels. The held-out split must
-       cover all four fault families and all three formulation families.
-    7. Set contrast_fixture_complete_score=1 only when all 36 pairs are
-       terminal, both authorities agree, and every hash replays. Set
-       label_balance_ready_score=1 only when each split is exactly balanced,
-       source-disjoint, and nonconstant.
-    8. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, artifact validation,
-       adversarial verification, row-consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.
-    9. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific
-       principle per required field and both contrast_fixture_complete_score
-       and label_balance_ready_score; preconditions_checked;
-       inference_substrate (deterministic_z3_contrast_fixture_no_llm);
-       duration_s; source_artifact_hashes; source_manifest_rows;
-       source_manifest_hash; rows; per_pair_results; per_candidate_rows;
-       mutation_attempt_rows; fault_family_rows; z3_authority_rows;
-       enumeration_authority_rows; authority_agreement_rows;
-       alpha_rename_rows; serialization_blinding_rows; split_rows;
-       split_hashes; label_balance_rows; source_overlap_rows;
-       expected_pair_count (36); observed_pair_count;
-       contrast_fixture_complete_score; label_balance_ready_score;
-       controlled_fixture_only (true); live_extraction_claimed (false);
-       random_seed; reproducibility_checksum; gate_check_summary with failed
-       check, expected value, and observed value for any blocked verdict;
-       verifier_is_oracle (true); verdict_class
-       (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial);
-       honest_verdict with a terminal prefix consistent with verdict_class.
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6984_exact_contrast_fixture.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
