-- id: exp6985-chronological-constraint-stream
-  title: Sealed chronological constraint-shift stream
-  track: self-learning
-  priority: critical
-  agent_type: codex
-  model: gpt-5.6-sol
-  requires_gpu: false
-  max_turns: 50
-  estimated_wall_time_min: 90
-  per_unit_rows: true
-  prior_failures:
-    - experiment_id: exp6678-constraint-family-stream
-      verdict: "blocked_fixture_gate: exact constraint-family stream is not ready"
-      addressed_by: "Exp6985 consumes Exp6984's newly balanced exact contrasts, seals tied and shifted event groups prospectively, and publishes every future-support checkpoint before online use."
-      retire_if_same_verdict: true
-  milestone: 2026.09.612
-  deliverable: results/experiment_6985_chronological_constraint_stream.json
-  gated_on:
-    - upstream: exp6984-exact-contrast-fixture
-      artifact_field: contrast_fixture_complete_score
-      op: '=='
-      value: 1
-  prompt: |
-    CONTEXT:
-    Exp6984 supplies balanced static contrasts. Continuous learning also needs a
-    sealed chronological stream with changing fault families, tied groups, and
-    later recurrence. V611's transactional memory tied its controls because the
-    stream never changed their decisions. This task creates the evaluation
-    stream only. It performs no online update.
-
-    Work at {project_root}. The execution date is {date}.
-
-    EXISTING CODE TO READ FIRST:
-    - {project_root}/CLAUDE.md and {project_root}/CODEX.md
-    - {project_root}/research-program.md section Continuous Self-Learning
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6984_exact_contrast_fixture.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6961_certified_event_sequence.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6967_certified_error_headroom_fixture.json
-    - {project_root}/results/experiment_6978_transactional_constraint_self_learning.json
-    - {project_root}/python/carnot/memory/transactional_constraint_memory.py
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/continuous-learning/spec.md
-    - {project_root}/openspec/capabilities/constraint-verification/spec.md
-    - {project_root}/research-references.md V612 Planner Refresh
-
-    TASK:
-    Build and seal a 24-event constraint-shift stream from source groups absent
-    from Exp6984. Include discriminative and tied candidate groups, freeze all
-    future-support checkpoints, and prove that no later label is visible in an
-    earlier event.
-
-    CONCRETE STEPS:
-    0. PRECONDITIONS: require contrast_fixture_complete_score=1, the frozen
-       fault operators, Z3, bounded enumeration, and at least 24 unused source
-       groups. On failure, write blocked_chronological_constraint_stream with
-       gate_check_summary.
-    1. Add REQ-LEARN-6985 and RED tests before implementation. Cover event
-       order, source disjointness, shift blocks, tie groups, future-label
-       sealing, recurrence, and bare chronological_stream_ready_score.
-    2. Freeze four ordered blocks of six events. Use a changed fault-family mix
-       in each block. Make the last block revisit the first block's families on
-       new sources so forgetting is measurable.
-    3. Create 16 one-positive/one-negative headroom events, four all-valid
-       events, and four all-invalid events. The tied groups test the required
-       no-update rule when exact group advantage is zero.
-    4. Certify every candidate with Z3 and bounded enumeration. Preserve
-       unknown and rejected construction attempts. Never replace an event after
-       any downstream task sees the stream hash.
-    5. Freeze event order, candidate order, exact labels, shift IDs, recurrence
-       links, retention anchors, held-future windows, and support metrics in an
-       immutable JSONL stream. Store labels in a separate sealed file.
-    6. For event t, construct a visibility manifest containing only data through
-       t-1. Prove by mutation tests that current and future labels cannot enter
-       the decision view.
-    7. Set chronological_stream_ready_score=1 only when all 24 events are
-       terminal, all authorities agree, event counts match, source overlap is
-       zero, and every visibility manifest replays.
-    8. Run focused tests, Ruff, OpenSpec coverage, artifact validation,
-       adversarial verification, row-consistency lint, and root-clutter checks.
-    9. REQUIRED ARTIFACT FIELDS: field_principles with one scientific
-       principle per required field and chronological_stream_ready_score;
-       preconditions_checked; inference_substrate
-       (deterministic_z3_chronological_stream_no_llm); duration_s;
-       source_artifact_hashes; source_disjointness_rows; stream_manifest;
-       stream_hash; sealed_label_path; sealed_label_hash; rows;
-       per_event_results; per_candidate_rows; shift_block_rows;
-       fault_family_rows; tie_group_rows; recurrence_rows;
-       retention_anchor_rows; held_future_window_rows;
-       visibility_manifest_rows; future_label_leakage_rows;
-       authority_agreement_rows; expected_event_count (24);
-       observed_event_count; headroom_event_count; all_valid_event_count;
-       all_invalid_event_count; chronological_stream_ready_score;
-       continuous_self_learning_fixture (true); random_seed;
-       reproducibility_checksum; gate_check_summary with failed check,
-       expected value, and observed value for any blocked verdict;
-       verifier_is_oracle (true); verdict_class
-       (positive | circular_positive | null | blocked | disqualified | partial);
-       honest_verdict with a terminal prefix consistent with verdict_class.
-
-    Run command: cd {project_root} && .venv/bin/python scripts/experiments/experiment_6985_chronological_constraint_stream.py --date {date}
-    Do NOT push. Do NOT modify scripts/research_conductor.py.
